{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LeverLogDerivative","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Filter.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.MeanValue"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.hasDerivAt_S_at_qstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.hasDerivAt_S_at_qstar","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L102-L115","doc":"**The S-slope at `q*` is exactly the pure static lever `A′/u(q*)³`**:\nbecause `A(q*) = 0`, the log-derivative correction of the\n`LeverLogDerivative` decomposition vanishes identically at `q*` — the\none-anchor derivative gate is exact there, for any `u`-derivative `u'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.eventually_sign_flip_S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.eventually_sign_flip_S","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L88-L100","doc":"**The S sign-flip across `q*`** — the \"hard fact\" of the S-leak audit\n(`S(muon) > 0 > S(proton)` with `q_p < q* < q_μ`), derived: the positive\nlever `u³` preserves the numerator's sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.eventually_sign_flip_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.eventually_sign_flip_A","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L64-L86","doc":"**The numerator sign-flips across `q*`** (simple zero, positive slope):\neventually on the punctured neighborhood, `A > 0` right of `q*` and `A < 0`\nleft of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.unlevered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.unlevered","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L57-L62","doc":"The un-levered identity `S·u³ = A` — the round-1 `r = S·u³` reframing,\nnow an algebraic consequence of the class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.slope_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.slope_pos","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The numerator slope at `q*` is positive (measured `A′ ≈ +2.37`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.deriv_at_qstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.deriv_at_qstar","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The numerator is differentiable at `q*` with derivative `A′`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.zero_at_qstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.zero_at_qstar","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The numerator vanishes at the decay-sector determination `q*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.u_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.u_pos","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The lever is positive (substrate `u = b·ℏ_q² > 0` for `q > 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.ladder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.ladder","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The ladder shape `S = A/u³` (the N=3 rung lever). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarOddLadderShape","kind":"class","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarOddLadderShape.lean#L37-L51","doc":"**Bar-odd ladder shape** (hypothesis carrier, §3b): `S = A/u³` with a\npositive lever `u`, a simple zero of the numerator at `q*`, and positive\nnumerator slope `A′` there.  All fields are the *measured/derived inputs*\nof the c₃ bar-odd chain; the theorems below are consequences. ","signatureChunk":0}]}